{"kind":"api","name":"worksheet.charts.add","summary":"Add a chart using a config object.","tags":["worksheet.charts.add"],"examples":[{"code":"const sheet = workbook.worksheets.add('Charts');\nconst chart = sheet.charts.add('line', {\n  title: 'Milky Way Star Birth Rate',\n  titleTextStyle: { fontSize: 18, bold: true },\n  categories: ['2020', '2021', '2022'],\n  series: [\n    { name: 'Milky Way', values: [1.8, 1.9, 2.0] },\n  ],\n  hasLegend: true,\n  legend: { position: 'top' },\n  barOptions: { direction: 'column', grouping: 'stacked', gapWidth: 120 },\n  dataLabels: { showValue: false },\n  from: { row: 1, col: 1 },\n  extent: { widthPx: 520, heightPx: 280 },\n});","summary":"Create a chart with a manual anchor"},{"code":"const sheet = workbook.worksheets.getItem('Charts');\nconst range = sheet.getRange('A2:B5');\nconst chart = sheet.charts.add('ColumnClustered', range, 'Auto');\nchart.title.text = 'Stock Prices and Market Caps';\nchart.setPosition(sheet.getRange('F2:M10'));\nchart.width = 500;\nchart.height = 300;\nchart.axes.valueAxis.majorGridlines.format.line.color = '#CCCCCC';","summary":"Compat range-anchored chart API"}],"notes":["Prefer passing a single config object to worksheet.charts.add(...) or assigning chart.xAxis/chart.yAxis/chart.legend/chart.dataLabels/chart.dataTable with compact config objects.","Config assignment merges; omitted fields keep their existing values (useful for incremental edits).","Skip noisy defaults in configs (e.g. text color is already theme text). Set only what changes the output.","Use either manual anchors ({ from, to/extent }) or the compat range overload.","Common chart types used in specs: 'bar', 'line', 'scatter'.","Config props used in specs: title, titleTextStyle, categories, series, hasLegend, legend, barOptions, xAxis, yAxis, dataLabels, dataTable.","Charts use 0-based row/col anchors for manual positioning.","Charts support title.text, setPosition, width/height, and axes.valueAxis/categoryAxis."]}
{"kind":"api","name":"worksheet.getRange","summary":"Get a Range using A1 notation.","tags":["worksheet.getRange"],"examples":[{"code":"const sheet = workbook.worksheets.getItem('Sheet1');\nconst range = sheet.getRange('A1:C10');","summary":"Create a range from A1 notation"}],"notes":["A1 patterns: A1, A1:C10, A:A (entire column), 2:2 (entire row).","Sheet names with spaces in formulas should be quoted: 'Cost Summary'!A1."]}
{"kind":"api","name":"worksheet.getCell","summary":"Get a single cell by zero-based row and column.","tags":["worksheet.getCell"],"examples":[{"code":"const sheet = workbook.worksheets.getItem('Sheet1');\nconst cell = sheet.getCell(1, 4);\ncell.values = [['Hello']];","summary":"Access a single cell by index"}],"notes":["Row and column are 0-based indexes.","Returns a Range representing a single cell."]}
{"kind":"api","name":"worksheet.freezePanes","summary":"Freeze or unfreeze worksheet panes.","tags":["freeze panes","freeze_panes","freeze_rows","freeze_columns","unfreeze","worksheet.freezePanes"],"examples":[{"code":"const sheet = workbook.worksheets.getItem('Data');\nsheet.freezePanes.freezeRows(1);\nsheet.freezePanes.freezeColumns(2);","summary":"Freeze header row and first two columns"}]}
{"kind":"api","name":"worksheet.showGridLines","summary":"Worksheet gridline visibility surface.","tags":["show_grid_lines","showGridLines","grid lines","gridlines","worksheet.show_grid_lines","worksheet.showGridLines"]}
{"kind":"api","name":"data-tables","summary":"What-if data tables for formulas.","tags":["tables","table","worksheet.tables","tables.add","data tables add","data_tables.add","data-tables"],"notes":["Use worksheet.dataTables.add('C2:E5', { rowInput, columnInput }) with the formula in the top-left cell of the range.","Data tables require at least a rowInput or columnInput."]}
